ion/id #uuid "a844b5df-969a-5ad4-9ad2-fd01250ec5ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-12212" :question/problem "![](images/c2/c2406e6f3cb76f50bfcc73a348b38d93b7a24da8e4314e0b3523bb4cbf143364.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OB}=b$, and $T$ divides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ in the ratio $AT:TB=1:1.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OT}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{AT}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OAB,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-a+b \\\\  & =b-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AT:TB=1:1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AT}=\\frac{1}{2}\\overset{\\to }{AB}=\\frac{1}{2}(b-a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OT} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT} \\\\  & =a+\\frac{1}{2}(b-a) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}a+\\frac{1}{2}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b42e7ab-ac63-5783-9fe9-b799c27fa880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "OR^(→) = \\frac{3}{4}p + \\frac{1}{4}q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095365} {:answer/id #uuid "92f11bab-00ea-5806-85db-1bdf7b4a1d64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "OR^(→) = \\frac{2}{3}p + \\frac{1}{3}q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095366} {:answer/id #uuid "ae89d302-f0f7-5e09-9194-c33771847064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "OR^(→) = \\frac{1}{2}p + \\frac{1}{2}q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095367} {:answer/id #uuid "db7890bf-209c-5d9f-a75a-7bb34f398293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "OR^(→) = \\frac{1}{3}p + \\frac{2}{3}q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095368} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb7d370-156f-57c3-abfb-39c1d9