\\frac{1}{3}u+\\frac{2}{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327054} {:answer/id #uuid "12bc31bd-410e-5cec-b3e8-db5ec16e6668" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{7}{9}v-\\frac{2}{9}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327095} {:answer/id #uuid "1d8032c3-8159-562d-b85e-ce01f3a9419c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{7}{9}u+\\frac{2}{9}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327189} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd9827b-fe26-5576-843d-788fca86322f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{2}{3}u+\\frac{1}{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328732} {:answer/id #uuid "f6116bad-8f2c-5913-918c-8429cac9d1d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=-\\frac{1}{3}v+\\frac{2}{3}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d8032c3-8159-562d-b85e-ce01f3a9419c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{7}{9}u+\\frac{2}{9}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327189} :answer-field/id #uuid "624e21c0-b503-5eed-93a7-5e549f2e0d0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329358}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cfe5446c-2b26-5e48-974b-de364027f648" :question/math-academy-id "q-42669" :question/problem "![](images/04/040127594f639248736d4492f1853bcb1e6ef18c37db9242ebe466045713628a.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=u,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OV}=v$ and $W$ divides $\\overset{―}{UV}$ in the ratio $UW:WV=2:7.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OW}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=u,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{UW}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OUV,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =\\overset{\\to }{UO}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-u+v \\\\  & =v-u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $UW:WV=2:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{UW}=\\frac{2}{9}\\overset{\\to }{UV}=\\frac{2}{9}(v-u).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OW} & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =u+\\frac{2}{9}(v-u) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{9}u+\\frac{2}{9}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20a4ecfa-47e2-56f4-a423-468e55f93529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{1}{2}h+\\frac{1}{2}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387003} {:answer/id #uuid "e23408c0-6a35-5afe-abe2-00bbdaf4622a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{4}h+\\frac{1}{4}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387004} {:answer/id #uuid "a498dbcf-0f77-508b-9c07-efe06b97d9ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{5}{8}h+\\frac{3}{8}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387005} {:answer/id #uuid "748b1bc5-d773-5fa4-a285-111048597c9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{1}{8}h+\\frac{3}{4}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387006} {:answer/id #uuid "86f8cb36-0676-5c61-8d2f-37ebe1006578" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{8}h+\\frac{5}{8}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86f8cb36-0676-5c61-8d2f-37ebe1006578" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{8}h+\\frac{5}{8}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387007} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c4f4208-0c8e-57ef-ad8c-1decee05823d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387002}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0b691a2-9da7-5f9d-b601-8f5daf61f352" :question/math-academy-id "q-120304" :question/problem "![](images/65/6560a7f05ae95638cbfe902dfa022b2d8de6b07c6e1e6f85051ccf87b92ec338.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OI}=i$ and $J$ divides $\\overset{―}{HI}$ in the ratio $HJ:JI=5:3.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OHI,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HI} & =\\overset{\\to }{HO}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-h+i \\\\  & =i-h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $HJ:JI=5:3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{HJ}=\\frac{5}{8}\\overset{\\to }{HI}=\\frac{5}{8}(i-h).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OJ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ} \\\\  & =h+\\frac{5}{8}(i-h) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}h+\\frac{5}{8}i.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390558 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6c08254-bcec-5457-b88b-bb1b31577752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\frac{5}{6}r+\\frac{1}{6}s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390560} {:answer/id #uuid "86737275-5bda-5fe0-92b5-103129881f25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\frac{6}{11}r+\\frac{5}{11}s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390561} {:answer/id #uuid "361d2b59-2e0b-5aa1-b524-15d353a4c2a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OV}=r+\\frac{5}{6}s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390562} {:answer/id #uuid "b20f5119-753b-5441-bf91-ce6580448a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\frac{5}{11}r+\\frac{6}{11}s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390563} {:answer/id #uuid "04d1bf75-797e-5041-b68d-706cd3bf0bc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\frac{1}{11}r+s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b20f5119-753b-5441-bf91-ce6580448a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\frac{5}{11}r+\\frac{6}{11}s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390563} :answer-field/id #uuid "48dac603-f4ce-5e8e-b8da-9de99fd610ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390559}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c822bdd5-b239-5109-a43e-980b6e32d798" :question/math-academy-id "q-278288" :question/problem "![](images/ba/ba82c6b68026b0f4339c1e4fa01c4b1aa1b7aee74b74176f81bba1c0e1de259f.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=r,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OS}=s$ and $V$ divides $\\overset{―}{RS}$ in the ratio $RV:VS=6:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OV}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RV}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=r,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{RV}.$\n\nFirst, from $△ORS,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RS} & =\\overset{\\to }{RO}+\\overset{\\to }{OS} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{OS} \\\\  & =-r+s \\\\  & =s-r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $RV:VS=6:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RV}=\\frac{6}{11}\\overset{\\to }{RS}=\\frac{6}{11}(s-r).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OV} & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RV} \\\\  & =r+\\frac{6}{11}(s-r) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{11}r+\\frac{6}{11}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420465 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "747da426-8469-5cfb-b9c1-0f275aa12f5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{1}{4}a+\\frac{3}{4}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420450} {:answer/id #uuid "7870ed39-d3a3-5476-9037-af3a46374a41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{5}{8}a+\\frac{3}{8}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420451} {:answer/id #uuid "ac24f6e2-146b-56c4-926e-7b7b203e75f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{3}{8}a+\\frac{5}{8}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420454} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a4f00d-a543-5fec-976f-fd2b59d619f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{3}{4}a+\\frac{1}{4}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420458} {:answer/id #uuid "f78f9d21-45cd-5cd7-95b8-055e70bef457" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{7}{8}a+\\frac{1}{8}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7870ed39-d3a3-5476-9037-af3a46374a41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{5}{8}a+\\frac{3}{8}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420451} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cd7bc1d-4953-5e13-8ab6-2c158bebc612" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420462}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6fe46ce7-a162-566e-a261-116569794a12" :question/math-academy-id "q-120289" :question/problem "![](images/52/52e25ccc5b59b3eecd914c5b141e443475a5de58299404528d27f1fc85db97ea.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OB}=b$, and $T$ divides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ in the ratio $AT:TB=3:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OT}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{AT}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OAB,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-a+b \\\\  & =b-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AT:TB=3:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AT}=\\frac{3}{8}\\overset{\\to }{AB}=\\frac{3}{8}(b-a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OT} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT} \\\\  & =a+\\frac{3}{8}(b-a) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}a+\\frac{3}{8}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector That Satisfies a Ratio in Terms of Known Vectors"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096696 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096496 :question/id #uuid "e8b9014e-32cf-5f04-856c-7fd663bea50f" :question/math-academy-id "e-528" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $f'(x) - 3\\sin(2x) = 0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 3\\sin{2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050101 :topic/math-academy-id 1112 :topic/title "Integrating Exponential Functions Using Linear Substitution"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050489 :topic/math-academy-id 478 :topic/title "Integrating Trigonometric Functions Using Substitution"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050771 :topic/math-academy-id 443 :topic/title "Integration Using Substitution"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097118 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f651d57-fd13-5223-b101-19044f5a3b48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x) =-\\frac{11}{2}x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094682} {:answer/id #uuid "0c189129-a43b-5083-8426-a8d988b5bcfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x) = \\frac{11}{2} - C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094683} {:answer/id #uuid "441b0a08-b772-5959-b466-9ce911e9e6d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x) =-\\frac{11}{2}x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094684} {:answer/id #uuid "63128db0-6242-55ce-a386-75928939d9fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x) = \\frac{11}{2}x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094685} {:answer/id #uuid "7833225a-e7d7-58d8-a243-47f76b32d976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x) = 11x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094686}] :answer-field/id #uuid "702c2b7a-1035-57b4-98fc-9ee1ec455ef0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094681}] :question/id #uuid "e1c8faa6-71a3-52b0-9c4c-3e41ed01dd83" :question/math-academy-id "q-14245" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $f^{′}(x) + 11x = 0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097299 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a181c2-eaa7-54a0-8890-e935b4d4ff1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{2x}-2{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330015} {:answer/id #uuid "15c676e1-03b3-5352-b3b8-1386a7ac7b2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330129} {:answer/id #uuid "c78be5e7-440c-5080-aede-7717891b5955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331715} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb467dd-d851-57e6-ba23-4d6c40542276" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{2x}-2{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331773} {:answer/id #uuid "fd0ac1c2-8887-5016-9ea9-5bc26155b0dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4{e}^{2x}-2{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15c676e1-03b3-5352-b3b8-1386a7ac7b2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330129} :answer-field/id #uuid "7491e487-3ec6-578a-921d-573211c3741a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332412}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb82aa2f-3e4a-523a-94c2-c95aa3cb8ffa" :question/math-academy-id "q-50136" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{2x}=-2x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{2x}-2x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253531 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2628def8-9645-51de-9e8f-3993f1de42dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250883} {:answer/id #uuid "2e2afe8b-693c-5e5d-8ae5-7dd6c9ecac38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250948} {:answer/id #uuid "7e485acb-f298-517c-be2f-3047650c561f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251613} {:answer/id #uuid "ce428001-7345-56f1-b009-0b23f9dd54d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252376} {:answer/id #uuid "d492b169-b001-5d91-9313-3a1cdca45303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce428001-7345-56f1-b009-0b23f9dd54d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252376} :answer-field/id #uuid "21d3ab40-897b-52d6-935d-dd5cec3b2f88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252865}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b105cb3a-38a2-5c0a-8e78-f3632457e0c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-119032" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the derivative term is already isolated on the left:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253532 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171dcc35-2e96-5d00-9b3e-92b88f1e973d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250755} {:answer/id #uuid "2b19b8bd-9546-5cc0-9ed1-4c2a8ecedd85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{3}{(x-1)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250923} {:answer/id #uuid "437d8ac4-b175-5851-bcbe-f20b4b028b84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251118} {:answer/id #uuid "64d8f14f-2e7e-56a6-a247-99126b763397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{(3x-1)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251380} {:answer/id #uuid "e882ef4b-8f4d-553d-bbb5-65eff9191ac7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "171dcc35-2e96-5d00-9b3e-92b88f1e973d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250755} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1a55590-7e4d-59c4-88a9-f483aed246b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253190}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e46bf143-4783-5ce4-a8e4-31db596b41d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-119034" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{3}{x-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the derivative term is already isolated on the left:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{3}{x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253533 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "245c51d3-f742-5f41-b1dd-3551a892b046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250868} {:answer/id #uuid "688f1217-b625-5da8-a08e-dadadf44274e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251410} {:answer/id #uuid "705ba4e9-a328-506c-95e2-3f7a3275a47d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)={x}^{2}(2x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251470} {:answer/id #uuid "9b76e6cf-b140-5d7b-bf6a-f55d3ab8cc9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)={x}^{2}(2-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251893} {:answer/id #uuid "cd912817-d2f0-5ce1-a2a2-c2744159033c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(3-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "245c51d3-f742-5f41-b1dd-3551a892b046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250868} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbaa4233-2442-5788-bdba-a93b2096247b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253180}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fb6cc49c-88f2-58a8-a4b7-b8174a349cdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-119035" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)+6{x}^{2}=4x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4x-6{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4x-6{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3}+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362335 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07dc3b58-eba0-5097-b69a-33c5acc27717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360865} {:answer/id #uuid "190d9a53-3469-5e7f-b03f-2cf38a49c79d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360936} {:answer/id #uuid "404a584d-5be0-5c62-874f-3e3012cc296c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361125} {:answer/id #uuid "46d918e7-6c1c-54ae-9afa-2a28c3b9aae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361143} {:answer/id #uuid "d39f0726-0e78-5f3d-a8ec-67d31d858e0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d39f0726-0e78-5f3d-a8ec-67d31d858e0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361784} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bf37d9f-29ab-5f48-be79-4562eb844e34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362036}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d1695f8e-4929-5966-a2ac-c737d784a8b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-99006" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $-5{f}^{′}(x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\int \\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int \\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386896 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1101527-9f4f-5301-a5d7-2c4675ea434d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)={e}^{x-3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386898} {:answer/id #uuid "702773f0-c93f-5fdc-8cfc-c4f417f927cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386899} {:answer/id #uuid "db2dc2fe-2a07-5f7b-a570-4e58c725722c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=3{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386900} {:answer/id #uuid "09cf98b5-cc32-56bd-a7bc-80017c397c1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)={e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386901} {:answer/id #uuid "2723b2b5-87a6-52a2-bd3a-988db461edac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-{e}^{-x/3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db2dc2fe-2a07-5f7b-a570-4e58c725722c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=3{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386900} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5995d24-fede-525d-a40c-73179ae79979" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386897}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57dad966-30e8-503a-bfa2-6fa76bd6e7c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-119033" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)+3{e}^{-x}=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-3{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-3{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-3\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3(-{e}^{-x})+C \\\\  & =3{e}^{-x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73b6602d-f037-52b0-8c48-d0885dedafc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2(x+9{e}^{-3x})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399991} {:answer/id #uuid "30b063ed-08ab-5694-9771-9427e9a07c6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=x-2{e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399992} {:answer/id #uuid "95477359-7c43-51b4-a1ff-890600150acd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=x+{e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399993} {:answer/id #uuid "4a2d9c2f-bf87-54d1-a5c5-0103894f75e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=x-18{e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399994} {:answer/id #uuid "3694a7a7-cd54-5712-bdcb-421abc079139" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2(x-3{e}^{-3x})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30b063ed-08ab-5694-9771-9427e9a07c6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=x-2{e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399992} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f36605a-43ff-547f-a708-ab078c73b400" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399990}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e422fe9-fc97-5df0-b6a5-ce1fd6f9f5cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-119037" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)-6{e}^{-3x}=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =1+6{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+6{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x+6\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x+6(-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3x}) \\\\  & =x-2{e}^{-3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096697 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096497 :question/id #uuid "a8e6c58c-da62-5dab-8325-a53c14d9b8ba" :question/math-academy-id "e-529" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d^2 y}{\\textrm d x^2} = x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}+Cx+D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$ We cannot combine them, because $C$ is being multiplied by $x$ while $D$ is not."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097300 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89aee0c2-41c4-50d9-95e7-d07999f8e43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5x^{2} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095725} {:answer/id #uuid "a8264bab-88eb-5c1b-8cf6-4b5658e50c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Cx^{2} + 10x + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095726} {:answer/id #uuid "c8066636-9a63-5ade-85aa-07f7e0be5cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095727} {:answer/id #uuid "0a099fae-b25d-5abb-a50a-c5dc1eda7e34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095728} {:answer/id #uuid "1a40f9c2-33a9-5233-bec8-c51acd272979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095729}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8c860608-75a8-5451-a1a7-a0683cdbc84f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29a4235d-41c9-5a0e-b658-3ec6b027584e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{2}+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398891} {:answer/id #uuid "4b317621-35b4-53d1-939d-fab67d8f1031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398892} {:answer/id #uuid "6dcf3415-556b-53c7-ac6f-21a5ddefd845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398893} {:answer/id #uuid "a552a9bb-4de8-5448-90ec-372d3554e55d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398894} {:answer/id #uuid "fa85c5fe-d852-5230-88fd-53d91e4bcd53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C{x}^{2}+10x+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b317621-35b4-53d1-939d-fab67d8f1031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398892} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1789600-f409-5b68-8f83-26b29073f519" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398890}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17751a3b-ed4b-5966-a450-330460c02715" :question/math-academy-id "q-50139" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=-10.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-10\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-10x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-10x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-10\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D \\\\  & =-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097301 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a745d53-2adc-5935-a97d-5a586599fa37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{1}{3}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095731} {:answer/id #uuid "f4387418-5075-52c7-b685-924f2791a4be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx^{2} + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095732} {:answer/id #uuid "035eddbc-75fb-53ba-bc61-c5e0c4f3f025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095733} {:answer/id #uuid "12887777-c8a6-5e16-bf30-ed290559c1e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx^{2} + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095734} {:answer/id #uuid "7a68fbfe-8f1c-512a-8cc2-1b00fe18af49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{3}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095735}] :answer-field/id #uuid "1b5a4615-20d2-563a-8738-3f3905aa1549" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae67e9eb-7a6a-5f1f-9633-a869be11af9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398897} {:answer/id #uuid "1e9d1539-56f7-56d2-9de6-1e9901343c60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398898} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9ac46a-1dd6-5423-b497-fd6f6d213a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398899} {:answer/id #uuid "bd19773a-598c-5d4a-9935-ec0892a47ffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398900} {:answer/id #uuid "89be7220-c09b-594d-8bff-c3a06f0b9221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb9ac46a-1dd6-5423-b497-fd6f6d213a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398899} :answer-field/id #uuid "30eeac9f-d833-5bc8-934f-4097337092f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398896}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e04bc45-f34f-56fc-9a0e-8643597c4852" :question/math-academy-id "q-50148" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-{e}^{3x}=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}\\,{e}^{3x})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253534 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "222d3811-c9d6-5e7d-b85c-95aa3edf1f5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-x}+Dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250846} {:answer/id #uuid "2aeffcd6-4797-59ec-860f-11aa268d3482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250918} {:answer/id #uuid "65573541-1d72-5f2c-8753-db5f49766c66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251383} {:answer/id #uuid "849fa2e5-06fb-57df-930c-0b02e73c0378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-x}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251665} {:answer/id #uuid "dd1f009d-922c-586a-8478-6e8b8c14b8c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2aeffcd6-4797-59ec-860f-11aa268d3482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250918} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdcccacb-a603-583d-bd6c-044e60d286f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253159}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31249dfd-dd0f-51ef-9508-c411dcb82eb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-119038" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=8{e}^{-2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\int {e}^{-2x}\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x})+C \\\\  & =-4{e}^{-2x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{-2x}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-4(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x})+Cx+D \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253535 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a7a8ec6-3a7f-59a8-a36a-57b3c0e72d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251298} {:answer/id #uuid "7c79b537-ac7c-5f96-ac1d-d1860fe46a0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251588} {:answer/id #uuid "bf97146c-f829-59ef-a419-71c2a32c9365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252244} {:answer/id #uuid "caaff75b-db1f-5d6d-9954-596535269be7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252349} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a50774-5155-52c7-ab4f-ad427a04fce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a7a8ec6-3a7f-59a8-a36a-57b3c0e72d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251298} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dba1b47-1418-53b5-8e0b-75806451ee28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252943}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39f64cb7-5a70-5fc4-8565-289e61a98a66" :question/math-academy-id "q-119041" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-8\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-8(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =4\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+Cx+D \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253536 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52771b76-d1b4-51e6-ab25-23d4a36b8b91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=16{e}^{x/2}+{x}^{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251227} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ba7691-e0f5-58b0-8306-ebfe9995ce2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=16{e}^{x/2}-3{x}^{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252144} {:answer/id #uuid "d52fa157-a79b-5633-8056-0ad742ff72b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=8{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252440} {:answer/id #uuid "dad3e85e-1ff8-5404-b11a-42ecf755a4c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=32{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252477} {:answer/id #uuid "e75f3c4e-0901-518a-8832-fdbd533170dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=32{e}^{x/2}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dad3e85e-1ff8-5404-b11a-42ecf755a4c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=32{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252477} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bc11b9f-979a-5428-873c-d6f95fed2f3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253046}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4f306795-58e9-56b9-bfb8-50791b341767" :question/math-academy-id "q-119042" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+6x=8{e}^{x/2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=8{e}^{x/2}-6x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (8{e}^{x/2}-6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int {e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8(2{e}^{x/2})-6(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+C \\\\  & =16{e}^{x/2}-3{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (16{e}^{x/2}-3{x}^{2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =16\\int {e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =16(2{e}^{x/2})-3(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})+Cx+D \\\\  & =32{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253537 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23cc8ac7-5e09-54ce-b6d3-e159d67ab8ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250861} {:answer/id #uuid "5901205a-e2f9-52f3-b94e-a09bbbbe0521" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{4}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251285} {:answer/id #uuid "60767b47-bf28-5927-9170-56b9e257c34c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{4}-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251342} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4e1b67-45cb-51ac-a61f-ee18bbb149b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252358} {:answer/id #uuid "f4155827-e220-55c0-a8b5-d48c90df5a62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-4{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc4e1b67-45cb-51ac-a61f-ee18bbb149b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252358} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeb1d879-87da-5436-bd2a-6290c0abb0e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253110}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5323a95-ccb4-5698-8e94-ec2b6a694be3" :question/math-academy-id "q-119043" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5=6{x}^{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-5.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-5)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-5x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-5x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-5x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-5(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061e9049-685a-5e57-b12d-6b56030be323" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250602} {:answer/id #uuid "42b59196-b9a8-573b-be83-9fd902357365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={2}^{x}{ln}^{2}⁡2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251109} {:answer/id #uuid "b5960315-6cae-5802-922d-5b341c99ee9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252150} {:answer/id #uuid "c18c981b-dd26-58f1-bd40-912972cd4a5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252261} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e95291-17f3-571b-b000-bb1e43ebce08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "061e9049-685a-5e57-b12d-6b56030be323" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250602} :answer-field/id #uuid "e27e7bd7-eaed-55b0-916c-a3dd3a5a5d99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253193}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4f9dee74-c92e-5523-b157-7ba038c745c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119044" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-{2}^{x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{2}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{2}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3120f347-6512-51ba-8814-9e94e5b4f3e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330382} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce95280-683d-5e12-8dc4-4bd3c4dab2ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330490} {:answer/id #uuid "3f867192-f0f3-5837-8919-076f5a3bf835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330514} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3c8989-f6d0-5647-ba9e-eebb2011d570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{4}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332030} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd989d0-88b5-5bdf-841b-6beef220f5ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ce95280-683d-5e12-8dc4-4bd3c4dab2ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330490} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc205ab-aa57-5042-9e55-6ce79c5b03ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332381}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d572743-1005-5db1-a849-a7030811290a" :question/math-academy-id "q-50146" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $x\\cdot \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-4x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-4(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-2(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4239f824-0cdb-56c2-b03e-ba26979ede69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{5}\\,{x}^{3/2}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345918} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0b8e6e-4ec7-58f9-81fa-5762778dd80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346028} {:answer/id #uuid "517c9cdb-fafc-50c3-8c25-73b1c9f3a696" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346052} {:answer/id #uuid "8b73bf1b-fafc-5923-a918-fb2d34e27d58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346559} {:answer/id #uuid "995de1a6-1b5d-505e-b32d-431f2c275661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{3}\\,{x}^{3/2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f0b8e6e-4ec7-58f9-81fa-5762778dd80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346028} :answer-field/id #uuid "a14bd67c-bf99-5b34-a9b6-546acd076bc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347887}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49effcbe-cf5f-52f7-9899-b28e9803c299" :question/math-academy-id "q-79554" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{x}=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\sqrt{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{2}{3}\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{2}{5}\\,{x}^{5/2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398200 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2339eddd-c520-53fc-835c-406bf5642b8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{5}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398202} {:answer/id #uuid "6cfc929f-0e67-5e47-80b6-d2949d1be4b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{x}^{4}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398203} {:answer/id #uuid "4dd5ffc9-d74f-592b-a383-53ba3803f136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{5}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398204} {:answer/id #uuid "395e4984-cf1d-534b-b01f-09b03aa00ba5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{x}^{5}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398205} {:answer/id #uuid "796c5808-234b-5385-a5e5-513d3b55563c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{x}^{4}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dd5ffc9-d74f-592b-a383-53ba3803f136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{5}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398204} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7d8f65-a93b-5daa-b8fa-34a0b4f4a5ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398201}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f503fbb-9abb-5178-8aa2-5b5187c150ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-119039" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=20{x}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =20\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =20\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+C \\\\  & =5{x}^{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5{x}^{4}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+Cx+D \\\\  & ={x}^{5}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "badd1b57-14e7-5b56-b3e2-4f76bf483962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399338} {:answer/id #uuid "0cc1b791-33fe-5cbe-8db2-7cec317b3415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399339} {:answer/id #uuid "9947a22d-6748-5635-9bff-c054c9d5412e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399340} {:answer/id #uuid "a32a5598-4875-50b4-a207-219749ce447a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399341} {:answer/id #uuid "39ea83b4-6e8e-5133-9645-9dd52053a38b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "badd1b57-14e7-5b56-b3e2-4f76bf483962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399338} :answer-field/id #uuid "76d542a7-e1e6-5040-8811-6896030adc94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399337}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "99338d6e-762d-5e46-924e-c9b8ff055bcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-99009" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=4x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=2x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096698 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096498 :question/id #uuid "ab40a4d3-c418-5b64-a04c-bb017155a4d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-530" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $y'  = 2x,$ and sketch the solution curves of this equation." :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\ny = x^2+C.\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,1.$\n\n![](images/e3/e37771799ef5fadc259e6ea0073042a83e0974b5a2619d1af3e87a7467e6d780.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23